{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110820","id":2853561762,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6qFeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110820","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110820.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110820.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110820","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110820/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110820/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110820/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/b92ffadee432756500bec64cdbccdfab6e7620b3","number":110820,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add PCK loading from memory","user":{"login":"0xcafeb33f","id":17749567,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzQ5NTY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17749567?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xcafeb33f","html_url":"https://github.com/0xcafeb33f","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xcafeb33f/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xcafeb33f/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xcafeb33f/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xcafeb33f/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xcafeb33f/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xcafeb33f/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xcafeb33f/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xcafeb33f/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xcafeb33f/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Adds `load_resource_pack_from_buffer` as an in-memory alternative to `load_resource_pack`.\r\n\r\nCloses godotengine/godot-proposals#5389.\r\n\r\nI made several implementation decisions that I would like feedback on and am open to modifying if desired: \r\n- This code was written with the goal of not breaking backwards-compatibility for public functions. If it is acceptable to change `PackedData::add_pack` to accept a `Ref<FileAccess>` instead of a path, that would greatly simplify this code and remove some mostly-duplicated functions.\r\n- The struct `PackedFile` was also left as-is for backwards-compatibility. This necessitated creating internal file paths (chosen to start with `mem://`) for downstream functions to read from, which also slightly slows performance for the new `from_buffer` function by requiring an additional hash of the buffer array. If it is acceptable to change `PackedFile` by replacing the pack path, then it would lead to a simpler and more efficient implementation.\r\n- The function `FileAccessMemory::register_file` is used for storing buffers long-term. Although it seems to work for this purpose, I could not find any other use or documentation of this function in the repository. Is it deprecated? Alternatives to `register_file` include storing the `Ref<FileAccess>` inside `PackedFile` (could be a problem for disk files if the file handle is closed and needs to be reopened), or creating a static local variable inside `FileAccessPack` that holds all buffers loaded.\r\n- `try_open_pack_from_buffer` was added as a purely virtual function to `PackSource`. There are lots of alternatives, but this would only really be a compatibility issue if users are inheriting from `PackSource` in their own classes (which I am not aware of).\r\n- Loading `ZipArchive` from buffer is still not supported. A different API would have to be used for this (`inflate` instead of `unzOpen2`?) and it was not mentioned in the original proposal.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/g